.TH "WMBlueCPU" "1" "0.4" "Draghicioiu Mihai Andrei" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
WMBlueCPU \- a dockapp which displays cpu usage
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
wmbluecpu [OPTIONS]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
\fBWMBlueCPU\fP is a cpu monitoring dockapp for window managers which support dockapps. It shows the current cpu usage with numbers and a graphical history list.
.SH "OPTIONS"
The following options can be passed to WMBlueCPU on the command line:
.TP 
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display basic usage info and exit
.TP 
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version number and exit
.TP 
.B \-display <DISPLAY>
The X11 display to connect to.
.TP 
.B \-m <MILISECS>
The number of miliseconds between screen updates
.TP 
.B \-w, \-\-window
Run in own window (also good for other windowmanagers)
.TP 
.B \-nw, \-\-no\-window
Don't run in own window
.TP 
.B \-s, \-\-shape
Use the XShape extension
.TP 
.B \-ns, \-\-no\-shape
Don't use the XShape extension. The window will be placed on it's own panel.
